{"ts":"2026-10-10T08:29:36.862Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"tool","toolName":"read_files","toolCallId":"toolu_018jcYfMU5w5q2F85JzCKFp2","output":[{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\.cline-runs\\run-134715-f3yl.task.md","result":"1 | # Instructions for Cline run run-134715-f3yl (mode: act, model: Cline default, started 2026-10-10T08:17:15.787Z)\n2 | \n3 | Read .clinerules and memory-bank, then do tasks/NEXT.md. Read docs/schemes.md carefully first (it is the source of truth). Write tests first. Finish by updating tasks/LOG.md and committing.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\tasks\\NEXT.md","result":" 1 | # NEXT TASK: T1, core rule engine v2 (tests first)\n 2 | \n 3 | T0 reviewed: tests pass (3/3), and the commit is in. Answer to your question: `docs/sample-notice-orunodoi-oct2026.md` is intentional; it is demo input for **T3** (not T4).\n 4 | \n 5 | **Important changes since T0 (read before coding):**\n 6 | - `memory-bank/projectbrief.md` is now **v2** and `docs/schemes.md` is **rule packs v2** (provenance, verified vs provisional, two verdicts, defensive name matching, corrected widow pension 40–79 and ₹300).\n 7 | - The language changed: **Assamese default + English** (not Hindi).\n 8 | \n 9 | ## Step 0 (small, 5 min)\n10 | - Refresh `memory-bank/productContext.md`, `systemPatterns.md` and `activeContext.md` so they match brief v2 (two verdicts, provenance, Assamese).\n11 | - Switch the app title to \"KaagazCheck: কাগজ চেক\" with the tagline \"Check before you apply\" / \"আবেদনৰ আগতে পৰীক্ষা কৰক\", set `<html lang=\"as\">`, and update the smoke test accordingly.\n12 | \n13 | ## Then do `tasks/backlog/T1-core-engine.md` exactly (it is already updated for v2).\n14 | \n15 | **Done when:** everything in T1's \"Done when\" holds, plus Step 0 is done; LOG.md updated; committed \"T1: core rule engine v2\".","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\systemPatterns.md","result":" 1 | # System patterns\n 2 | \n 3 | ## Core pipeline: AI reads → rule engine decides → AI explains\n 4 | 1. **Read (AI):** a document image or text → `ExtractedDoc` (fields + per-field confidence), validated with zod.\n 5 | 2. **Decide (pure code):** `src/core/` rule engine takes `SchemeRule` + `ExtractedDoc[]` + `Answers` → `ReadinessReport`. Deterministic, unit- and property-tested. No model text ever decides a status.\n 6 | 3. **Explain (AI, optional):** friendlier wording or a letter draft, built only from the report's codes and fields.\n 7 | \n 8 | ## Module boundaries\n 9 | - `src/core/`: pure TypeScript (name matching, rule engine, schemas, scheme definitions). No React, network, DB or `process.env` imports.\n10 | - `src/server/ai.ts`: the **only** module that calls a model. Structured JSON output → zod validation → one retry → safe fallback. Logs the model, prompt version and an input hash (never raw personal data).\n11 | - `src/server/store.ts`: the **only** database writer (`node:sqlite`, WAL mode, transactions). Used from T3 for `scheme_proposals`.\n12 | - `src/server/agent/`: `@cline/sdk` Scheme Onboarding Agent (T3); its tools call into `src/core`.\n13 | - `src/app/api/**/route.ts`: thin route handlers with `export const runtime = \"nodejs\"`.\n14 | - `src/app/**`: UI. Calls API routes, never the model directly.\n15 | \n16 | ## Status vocabulary\n17 | - Check: `pass | fail | uncertain`.\n18 | - Report: `ready | fix_first | not_eligible | confirm_at_office`.\n19 | - Unclear rule or data → `uncertain` / `confirm_at_office`.\n20 | \n21 | ## Name matching (showcase)\n22 | Normalise (uppercase, strip punctuation, collapse spaces, drop honorifics) → expand abbreviations → Devanagari→Latin → Jaro-Winkler. Pass ≥ 0.92, uncertain 0.80–0.92, fail < 0.80. Initials never pass. See `docs/schemes.md`.\n23 | \n24 | ## Privacy\n25 | Aadhaar masked to the last 4 digits in UI, logs and printouts. Images are processed in memory only. Collect the minimum personal data.\n26 | \n27 | ## Testing\n28 | Vitest; fast-check property tests for the matcher and engine. Write tests first for core logic.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\activeContext.md","result":" 1 | # Active context\n 2 | \n 3 | ## Current state\n 4 | T0 (Memory Bank + scaffold) is done. The app is a placeholder home page titled \"KaagazCheck: कागज़ चेक\" with a smoke test.\n 5 | \n 6 | ## Decisions made in T0\n 7 | - Next.js 16.4.0 scaffolded in a temp folder and copied in (create-next-app refuses non-empty folders).\n 8 | - `src/` layout with `@/*` alias. Core logic lives in `src/core/`; the smoke test (`src/core/appInfo.test.ts`) also exercises zod and fast-check.\n 9 | - Vitest runs in the Node environment on `src/**/*.test.ts`; no jsdom or React rendering tests yet.\n10 | - `.gitignore`: ignores `.env`, `.env*.local`, `node_modules`, `.next`, `*.db`; keeps `.env.example` and `.cline-runs/` tracked.\n11 | - `<html lang=\"hi\">`; page title and description come from `src/core/appInfo.ts`.\n12 | \n13 | ## Next step\n14 | T1, core engine (`tasks/backlog/T1-core-engine.md`): schemas, name matcher, rule engine for the 3 schemes, tests first.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\progress.md","result":" 1 | # Progress\n 2 | \n 3 | ## Done\n 4 | - [x] T0: Memory Bank (productContext, systemPatterns, techContext, activeContext, progress), Next.js 16 scaffold (TS strict, Tailwind v4, ESLint), Vitest + fast-check + zod, npm scripts, `.gitignore`, `.env.example`, placeholder page, smoke test, first commit.\n 5 | \n 6 | ## To do\n 7 | - [ ] T1: core engine (types/zod schemas, name matcher, rule engine, 3 schemes, sample sets)\n 8 | - [ ] T2: main flow (scheme picker → documents → questions → readiness report, Hindi/English, AI gateway `src/server/ai.ts`)\n 9 | - [ ] T3: Scheme Onboarding Agent (`@cline/sdk`, `node:sqlite` store, admin approval)\n10 | - [ ] T4: rejection decoder + polish\n11 | - [ ] T-last: freeze, full README, demo path check\n12 | \n13 | ## Known issues\n14 | - `npm install` warns that eslint@9 is deprecated (it is the version create-next-app 16.4.0 pins with eslint-config-next). Harmless for now.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\tasks\\LOG.md","result":" 1 | # Build log (Cline appends after every task)\n 2 | \n 3 | ## T0: scaffold + memory bank (run-133358-c1ef, 2026-10-10)\n 4 | Followed the plan from run-133031-4cma.\n 5 | \n 6 | **Files created/changed**\n 7 | - Memory Bank: `memory-bank/productContext.md`, `systemPatterns.md`, `techContext.md`, `activeContext.md`, `progress.md` (`projectbrief.md` untouched).\n 8 | - Scaffold (create-next-app@16.4.0 in a temp folder, copied in): `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, `tsconfig.json` (strict), `next.config.ts`, `eslint.config.mjs` (+ ignores for `.cline-runs/`, `docs/`, `memory-bank/`, `tasks/`), `next-env.d.ts`, `AGENTS.md`, `public/*`, `src/app/{layout.tsx,page.tsx,globals.css,favicon.ico}`.\n 9 | - New: `src/core/appInfo.ts` (title/taglines, pure), `src/core/appInfo.test.ts` (smoke test, also exercises zod + fast-check), `vitest.config.mts`, `.env.example` (`CLINE_API_KEY=`, `CLINE_MODEL=`), `README.md` (short placeholder), `.gitignore` (ignores `.env`, `.env*.local`, `node_modules`, `.next`, `*.db*`; keeps `.env.example` and `.cline-runs/`).\n10 | - Deps added: `zod@^4.6.5`, dev `vitest@^5.0.3`, `fast-check@^4.10.2`, `@types/node@^22`.\n11 | - Scripts: `dev`, `build`, `start`, `lint` (`eslint .`), `typecheck` (`tsc --noEmit`), `test` (`vitest run`), `test:watch`.\n12 | \n13 | **Results**\n14 | - `npm test`: 1 file, 3 passed, 0 failed.\n15 | - `npm run typecheck`: pass. `npm run lint`: pass (0 problems). `npm run build`: pass (Next 16.4.0, Turbopack; `/` prerendered static).\n16 | - Verified the built HTML contains \"KaagazCheck: कागज़ चेक\" and `lang=\"hi\"`, and the CSS contains the Tailwind utilities used.\n17 | \n18 | **Deviations from the plan**\n19 | - `@types/node` bumped from `^20` to `^22` (Vitest 5 peer requirement; matches Node 22+).\n20 | - Vitest config is `.mts` instead of `.ts` (avoids a Vite ESM/CJS config warning).\n21 | - `layout.tsx` uses explicit `Readonly<{ children: React.ReactNode }>` instead of the generated global `LayoutProps<\"/\">`, so `typecheck` passes before `.next/types` exists.\n22 | - No `postcss.config.mjs`: create-next-app 16.4 wires Tailwind v4 via the `@tailwindcss/turbopack` loader in `next.config.ts`; Tailwind confirmed working in the build.\n23 | \n24 | **Open issues**\n25 | - npm warns `eslint@9` is deprecated (pinned by eslint-config-next 16.4.0) and that `unrs-resolver` has an unapproved postinstall script; neither blocks lint or build.\n26 | - `docs/sample-notice-orunodoi-oct2026.md` appeared in `docs/` during this run (not created by Cline); committed as-is with `git add -A`.\n27 | \n28 | **Requests for Claude**\n29 | - None blocking. Please confirm that `docs/sample-notice-orunodoi-oct2026.md` is intended for T4 (rejection decoder) and reference it in the task spec if so.","success":true}],"durationMs":7}}
