{"ts":"2026-10-10T08:29:40.856Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"tool","toolName":"read_files","toolCallId":"toolu_01ERPtLXM2QL5riuim2Ga7eZ","output":[{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\tasks\\backlog\\T1-core-engine.md","result":" 1 | # T1: Core rule engine v2, tests first (about 75 min)\n 2 | \n 3 | Mode: ACT. Pure TypeScript in `src/core/` only: no UI, network, AI or DB imports. **Read `docs/schemes.md` (rule packs v2) first; it is the source of truth.**\n 4 | \n 5 | 1. `src/core/types.ts` + zod schemas: `RuleProvenance`, `SchemeRule` (with `version`), `ExtractedDoc`, `Answers`, `Check`, `Report` (two verdicts: `eligibility`, `readiness`), as in memory-bank/projectbrief.md.\n 6 | 2. `src/core/schemes/pm-kisan.ts`, `orunodoi-3.ts`, `nsap-widow.ts`: data validated by `SchemeRule`. Every criterion and benefit has provenance with `status: verified | provisional` exactly as docs/schemes.md marks it. Question text in Assamese + English. Registry: `getScheme(id)`, `listSchemes()`, `registerScheme(rule)` (used by T3).\n 7 | 3. `src/core/nameMatch.ts` → `{ level: same | possible_match | initials_only | mismatch, score }` per docs/schemes.md. Normalisation, honorifics, abbreviations, transliteration of Devanagari and Assamese/Bengali script to Latin (basic table), Jaro-Winkler.\n 8 | 4. `src/core/age.ts`: age on an explicit `asOfDate`.\n 9 | 5. `src/core/aadhaar.ts`: `maskAadhaar()` → `XXXX XXXX 1234`.\n10 | 6. `src/core/benefit.ts`: `benefitOn(scheme, date)`, supporting time-bounded overrides (needed for the T3 demo).\n11 | 7. `src/core/evaluate.ts`: `evaluate(scheme, docs, answers, asOfDate) → Report`. Rules:\n12 |    - verified criterion failed → eligibility `not_eligible`\n13 |    - provisional criterion triggered → `needs_verification` (never not_eligible)\n14 |    - missing mandatory doc or a name `mismatch` → readiness `action_required`\n15 |    - `possible_match`, `initials_only`, low-confidence field, or any external check (bank seeding, account active, eKYC, land verified) → `needs_verification`\n16 |    - otherwise `ready_for_review`\n17 |    - Each check has `messageEn`, `messageAs`, `fixWhere`, `provenance`.\n18 | 8. `src/core/rejectionCodes.ts`: enum (`NAME_MISMATCH_AADHAAR`, `AADHAAR_NOT_SEEDED_BANK`, `INVALID_ACCOUNT_IFSC`, `ACCOUNT_INACTIVE`, `LAND_NOT_VERIFIED`, `EKYC_PENDING`, `PENDING_STATE_ACTION`, `UNKNOWN`) → fix steps in English + Assamese.\n19 | \n20 | **Tests (write first):**\n21 | - nameMatch: \"Ramesh Kumar\" vs \"RAMESH KUMAR \" → same; \"RAMESHKUMAR\" vs \"Ramesh Kumar\" → same; \"Smt. Sunita Devi\" vs \"SUNITA DEBI\" → possible_match; \"RAMESH KR SHARMA\" vs \"Ramesh Kumar Sharma\" → possible_match; \"R. Kumar\" vs \"Ramesh Kumar\" → initials_only; \"Rameshwar Sharma\" vs \"Ramesh Kumar Sharma\" → mismatch; \"Ramesh\" vs \"Suresh\" → mismatch.\n22 | - fast-check: a name is `same` as itself; level is symmetric; `maskAadhaar` never outputs more than 4 digits; **possible_match never yields an `ok` check**.\n23 | - evaluate, PM-KISAN: clean → ready_for_review with bank seeding as needs_verification; bank \"RAMESH KR SHARMA\" → needs_verification; land \"Rameshwar Sharma\" → action_required (fixWhere circle office); missing land_record → action_required; income tax yes → not_eligible; large landholding has NO effect (regression test for the removed 2-ha limit).\n24 | - evaluate, widow: age 39 → not_eligible; 40 → likely_eligible; 79 → likely_eligible; 80 → not_eligible; benefit centralShare 300; stateTopUp null.\n25 | - evaluate, Orunodoi: no ration card → action_required; four-wheeler yes → needs_verification (not not_eligible).\n26 | - benefitOn: Orunodoi with a 2026-10 override → 1500 in October, 1250 in November.\n27 | \n28 | **Done when:** all tests pass, typecheck clean, LOG.md updated, committed \"T1: core rule engine v2\".","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\docs\\schemes.md","result":" 1 | # Rule packs v2: the three schemes (corrected 10 Oct 2026)\n 2 | \n 3 | Source of truth for the rule engine. v2 applies corrections from a check against government sources: widow pension age and amount, PM-KISAN bank checks, and Orunodoi 3.0 rules downgraded to provisional.\n 4 | \n 5 | ## Golden rules for every rule\n 6 | 1. **Every rule carries provenance:** `sourceUrl`, `sourceTitle`, `clause` (if known), `effectiveDate` (if known), `verifiedOn` (2026-10-10), `version`, and `status: verified | provisional`.\n 7 | 2. **Provisional rules never give a definitive pass or fail.** They return `needs_verification` with \"confirm at the office\" and say what to ask.\n 8 | 3. **Document photos can't prove external facts.** Whether a bank account is active or Aadhaar-seeded, whether land is verified, whether eKYC is done: these are `needs_verification` (the user confirms, or checks the official status page), never `pass` from a photo.\n 9 | 4. **Fuzzy name matching never proves identity.** See \"Name consistency\" below.\n10 | 5. **Eligibility and readiness are reported separately.** Eligible ≠ application complete, and complete ≠ government approval.\n11 | 6. **Money values are versioned and split:** `centralShare`, `stateTopUp` (null = unconfirmed), `effectiveDate`, and `source`. Never show an unconfirmed total.\n12 | \n13 | ## Result model\n14 | - **Eligibility:** `likely_eligible` · `not_eligible` (a verified criterion failed) · `needs_verification`\n15 | - **Readiness:** `ready_for_review` (no known issues found by our checks) · `action_required` (mismatch, missing mandatory document, unmet verified criterion) · `needs_verification` (unclear image, provisional rule, external status we can't see)\n16 | - Each check has `{ id, result: ok | action_required | needs_verification | not_applicable, messageEn, messageAs, fixWhere, ruleProvenance }`.\n17 | - Wording promise: \"We help you catch preventable mistakes. We do not guarantee approval; the department decides.\"\n18 | \n19 | ---\n20 | \n21 | ## 1. PM-KISAN (id `pm-kisan`): the FLAGSHIP end-to-end demo\n22 | sourceUrl: https://pmkisan.gov.in/ · summary: https://en.vikaspedia.in/viewcontent/agriculture/policies-and-schemes/crops-related/comprehensive-guide-to-the-pradhan-mantri-kisan-samman-nidhi-(pm-kisan)-scheme?lgn=en · status: verified (core criteria)\n23 | \n24 | - Benefit: ₹6,000/year in 3 instalments of ₹2,000 by DBT (centralShare 6000/yr, stateTopUp 0).\n25 | - Eligible: a landholding farmer family (husband, wife, minor children) owning cultivable land per state land records, **regardless of holding size** (the earlier 2-hectare limit was removed in 2019). **Do not add any landholding-size limit.**\n26 | - Exclusions (verified; any \"yes\" → not_eligible): `holds_constitutional_post`, `govt_employee` (serving or retired; not MTS, Class IV or Group D), `income_tax_payer` (last assessment year), `practising_professional` (doctor, engineer, lawyer, CA, architect), `pension_10k_plus` (₹10,000+/month; not MTS, Class IV or Group D).\n27 | - Mandatory documents: `aadhaar`, `bank_passbook`, `land_record`.\n28 | - Document-level checks (our engine CAN decide): all mandatory docs present; name consistency across aadhaar, bank_passbook and land_record; IFSC format `^[A-Z]{4}0[A-Z0-9]{6}$`; account number present (9–18 digits); the land record shows the applicant (or a family member) as owner.\n29 | - External checks (always `needs_verification`, with how to check): Aadhaar seeded to the bank account (ask at the bank branch); account active; eKYC done (PM-KISAN portal OTP, or CSC biometric); land verified by the state.\n30 | \n31 | ## 2. Orunodoi 3.0, Assam (id `orunodoi-3`): local relevance, verified rules only\n32 | Official page: https://dhemaji.assam.gov.in/scheme-page/orunodoi (Govt of Assam, last updated 8 May 2025). Secondary: https://www.publicservicesmap.in/schemes/orunodoi-3.0--aos?lang=en\n33 | \n34 | **Verified (from the official page):**\n35 | - Benefit: ₹1,250/month to families with **valid ration cards** (centralShare 0, stateTopUp 1250, recurring). Note: a reported one-time ₹1,500 payment for October 2026 is a temporary change; don't treat it as the recurring amount.\n36 | - **No income certificate required** (official page says so).\n37 | - Mandatory: valid ration card. Preliminary selection is \"based on eligibility/ineligibility conditions\" through an undertaking-cum-checklist (Annexure A).\n38 | \n39 | **Provisional (secondary sources, or the 2020 original guideline; NOT confirmed for 3.0):**\n40 | - The NFSA enrolment precondition (myScheme lists it; the official page says \"valid ration card\").\n41 | - The eligibility any-of list (widow, PwD, AAY, household income under ₹2 lakh, etc.).\n42 | - The whole exclusion list (elected representatives, professionals, teachers, government staff and pensioners, contractors, traders, large landholders, four-wheeler owners, similar state cash schemes).\n43 | - Supporting documents (Aadhaar, bank passbook, voter ID, age proof, address proof, self-declaration).\n44 | \n45 | **Engine behaviour:** the ration card is a mandatory check (missing → action_required). Each provisional criterion is asked as a question, and any answer that would exclude → `needs_verification` (\"This may make you ineligible. Confirm at the Gram Panchayat.\"), never `not_eligible`. Supporting documents are shown as a checklist labelled \"commonly asked; confirm the current list\".\n46 | - Name consistency across ration_card, aadhaar and bank_passbook (if provided).\n47 | \n48 | ## 3. Widow Pension, IGNWPS under NSAP (id `nsap-widow`): the simple, reliable rule demo\n49 | sourceUrl: https://www.publicservicesmap.in/schemes/indira-gandhi-national-widow-pension-scheme--ignwps (aligns with the Ministry of Rural Development statement cited by the reviewer) · status: verified (age, BPL, central amount)\n50 | \n51 | - Eligible: widow, **age 40–79 inclusive**, household **BPL** per GoI criteria.\n52 | - Age: computed from the Aadhaar DOB **on an explicit `asOfDate`** (default today; injectable for tests).\n53 | - Benefit: **centralShare ₹300/month** (ages 40–79); stateTopUp for Assam = null (unconfirmed → show \"plus any state top-up; confirm locally\").\n54 | - Mandatory (provisional list; the source has no official document list): `aadhaar`, `death_certificate` (husband), `bank_passbook`; BPL proof. Mark the list as \"commonly required; confirm locally\".\n55 | - Checks: age window (verified → can say not_eligible); `bpl_household` question (no → not_eligible); name consistency across aadhaar and bank_passbook; death certificate present (missing → action_required).\n56 | - Age below 40 → not_eligible. Age 80+ → not_eligible for the widow pension band here; suggest checking the Old Age Pension (a scheme the agent can onboard in the demo).\n57 | \n58 | ---\n59 | \n60 | ## Name consistency (core showcase, defensive version)\n61 | Output levels, from strongest to weakest:\n62 | - `same`: identical after formatting normalisation (case, punctuation, extra spaces, joined vs spaced words, honorifics SHRI/SMT/MR/MRS/KUMARI/LATE). → check `ok`.\n63 | - `possible_match`: differs only by known abbreviations or variants (KR↔KUMAR, MD/MOHD↔MOHAMMAD, DEVI↔DEBI, SK↔SHEIKH), transliteration (Devanagari/Assamese/Bengali script ↔ Latin), or Jaro-Winkler ≥ 0.85 on the normalised form. → `needs_verification`: \"These look like the same person written differently. Officials may still reject this. Ask the bank/Aadhaar centre to make them identical.\"\n64 | - `initials_only`: \"R. KUMAR\" vs \"RAMESH KUMAR\" → `needs_verification`.\n65 | - `mismatch`: below that threshold (e.g. \"Rameshwar Sharma\" vs \"Ramesh Kumar Sharma\", \"Ramesh\" vs \"Suresh\") → `action_required`, saying which document to correct and where.\n66 | - The score is shown for transparency but **never** turns a check into `ok` by itself; only `same` does.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\projectbrief.md","result":" 1 | # Project brief v2: KaagazCheck (কাগজ চেক): \"Check before you apply\"\n 2 | \n 3 | **Pitch:** We help citizens catch preventable welfare-application mistakes *before* they submit their papers. Our AI reads the documents; a tested rule engine checks them; and Cline maintains the rules as official guidelines change.\n 4 | **Promise:** we reduce preventable errors. We do NOT guarantee approval; the department decides.\n 5 | \n 6 | ## Problem (evidence: docs/research.md)\n 7 | Eligible people lose benefits after applying because their documents disagree (name spellings across Aadhaar, bank and land record; account not Aadhaar-seeded; missing papers) or because rejections arrive unexplained. In Rajasthan in 2019, only about 23% of registered PM-KISAN farmers got the third instalment, mostly due to name mismatches with Aadhaar.\n 8 | \n 9 | ## Users\n10 | - **Citizen** in Assam on a basic Android phone, often helped by family or a CSC/NGO helper.\n11 | - **Rule maintainer** (helper organisation) who keeps scheme rules current using the Cline agent.\n12 | \n13 | ## Languages\n14 | **Assamese (default) + English toggle.** All fixed UI and check messages live in one `src/i18n.ts` with `as` and `en` keys. Assamese strings must be reviewed by a native speaker before the demo (Das will arrange). AI-generated Assamese (letters, explanations) is labelled \"draft\".\n15 | \n16 | ## Scope: rule packs v2 (docs/schemes.md is the source of truth)\n17 | - **PM-KISAN: flagship, full end-to-end demo** (name mismatch, missing document, uncertain bank status).\n18 | - **Orunodoi 3.0: Assam relevance, verified rules only;** provisional criteria → \"needs verification\".\n19 | - **Widow Pension (IGNWPS): simple, reliable rules** (age 40–79, BPL, central ₹300/month).\n20 | \n21 | ## Architecture (the trust design)\n22 | 1. **Document reader (AI):** extracts names, dates, account details and document type, with per-field confidence. Low confidence → user confirms.\n23 | 2. **Deterministic rule engine (pure code, tested):** normalises fields, checks consistency, evaluates verified criteria, finds missing documents. Provisional rules and external facts → `needs_verification`.\n24 | 3. **Two separate verdicts:** *Eligibility* (likely_eligible / not_eligible / needs_verification) and *Readiness* (ready_for_review / action_required / needs_verification).\n25 | 4. **Next steps:** corrections, where to go (bank, Aadhaar centre, circle office, Gram Panchayat), the source of each rule, and a printable cover sheet.\n26 | 5. **Explainer (AI, optional):** friendly wording in Assamese, built only from the engine's result.\n27 | \n28 | ## Core loop (must-ship demo path)\n29 | Pick scheme → add documents (photo, or \"Use sample A/B/C\") → confirm low-confidence fields → answer yes/no questions → two-verdict report with fixes and sources → print cover sheet.\n30 | Samples (clearly fake): A = clean PM-KISAN farmer → ready_for_review (+ bank seeding needs verification). B = PM-KISAN with \"RAMESH KR SHARMA\" (bank, possible match) and \"Rameshwar Sharma\" (land record, mismatch) → action_required. C = widow pension, missing death certificate → action_required.\n31 | \n32 | ## Cline inside the product: Rule Maintenance Agent (T3)\n33 | Upload or paste a scheme notice → a `@cline/sdk` Agent proposes a **rule change** (new scheme or edited rule, with provenance: sourceUrl, clause, effectiveDate) → writes **regression tests** → runs them through the engine (existing scheme tests must still pass) → shows a diff + test results → a **human approves** → a new rule-pack version is published (old version kept). Demo inputs: `docs/sample-guideline-ignoaps.md` (add a scheme) and `docs/sample-notice-orunodoi-oct2026.md` (a one-time payment change, to show versioning).\n34 | \n35 | ## Trust rules (non-negotiable)\n36 | - AI reads and explains; **code decides**. No eligibility claim from model text.\n37 | - Aadhaar masked to the last 4 digits everywhere; images processed in memory, never stored.\n38 | - Every rule carries provenance; provisional → needs_verification.\n39 | - A fuzzy name score never equals identity.\n40 | - Demo uses fake documents only.\n41 | \n42 | ## Data model sketch\n43 | - `RuleProvenance` { sourceUrl, sourceTitle, clause?, effectiveDate?, verifiedOn, version, status: verified | provisional }\n44 | - `SchemeRule` { id, version, nameEn, nameAs, benefit { centralShare, stateTopUp|null, period, effectiveDate, provenance }, mandatoryDocs[], supportingDocs[], ageRange?, eligibilityAnyOf[], exclusions[], externalChecks[], each criterion with provenance }\n45 | - `ExtractedDoc` { docType, fields { name, dob, aadhaarLast4, accountNo, ifsc, ownerNames[], husbandName, ... }, confidence per field }\n46 | - `Report` { eligibility, readiness, checks[], schemeVersion, asOfDate }\n47 | - DB (T3): `rule_versions` { schemeId, version, ruleJson, testsJson, testResultJson, status: proposed | published | rejected, sourceNote, createdAt, approvedAt }\n48 | \n49 | ## Stretch\n50 | Assamese voice readout (only if the browser has an as-IN voice; otherwise hide) · rejection-notice decoder (T4) · helper mode for many applicants.\n51 | \n52 | ## Cut list (cut in this order)\n53 | Voice → decoder letter drafting → real photo upload (keep samples + manual entry) → cover-sheet styling. **Never cut:** the two-verdict report, provenance, the Cline agent with tests + approval.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\productContext.md","result":" 1 | # Product context: KaagazCheck (कागज़ चेक)\n 2 | \n 3 | ## Why it exists\n 4 | Eligible people lose welfare benefits *after* applying: names that don't match across Aadhaar, bank and land records; Aadhaar not seeded to the bank; missing certificates; rejection reasons they cannot understand. Documented example: Rajasthan 2019, only about 23% of registered PM-KISAN farmers got the 3rd instalment, mostly because of Aadhaar name mismatches (sources in `docs/research.md`).\n 5 | \n 6 | KaagazCheck checks the papers **before** the person applies, in Hindi (English toggle), and says exactly what to fix and where.\n 7 | \n 8 | ## Users\n 9 | - **Citizen** (farmer, widow, woman of an Assam household) on a basic Android phone, often helped by a family member or a CSC/NGO helper.\n10 | - **Admin / helper organisation** that adds new schemes through the Scheme Onboarding Agent (Cline SDK).\n11 | \n12 | ## Schemes in scope\n13 | PM-KISAN (`pm-kisan`) · Orunodoi 3.0, Assam (`orunodoi-3`) · Widow Pension IGNWPS (`nsap-widow`). Rules are in `docs/schemes.md`.\n14 | \n15 | ## Main demo path (3 minutes)\n16 | 1. Pick a scheme.\n17 | 2. Add documents: upload a photo or tap \"Use sample\" (clean / name mismatch / missing document).\n18 | 3. AI reads each document → fields + confidence; low confidence → the user confirms or edits.\n19 | 4. Answer 3–5 yes/no exclusion questions.\n20 | 5. Rule engine → readiness report: 🟢 ready / 🔴 fix first / ⚪ not eligible / 🟡 confirm at office, each check with a reason, where to fix it and its source.\n21 | 6. Hindi report + printable cover sheet.\n22 | \n23 | ## Second mode\n24 | Rejection decoder (T4): rejection text → known reason code → fix steps + a drafted Hindi letter.\n25 | \n26 | ## Cline inside the product\n27 | Scheme Onboarding Agent (T3): guideline text → rule definition + test cases → run through the rule engine → **pending** proposal → a human approves.\n28 | \n29 | ## Trust rules\n30 | - The AI only reads and explains; the rule engine decides.\n31 | - Aadhaar is masked to the last 4 digits everywhere; uploaded images are processed in memory, never stored.\n32 | - When unsure, say \"confirm at the office\"; never guess.\n33 | - Demo uses fake sample documents only.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\src\\core\\appInfo.ts","result":" 1 | // Pure constants shared by the UI and tests. No UI, network or database imports.\n 2 | \n 3 | export const APP_NAME = \"KaagazCheck\";\n 4 | export const APP_NAME_HI = \"कागज़ चेक\";\n 5 | export const APP_TITLE = `${APP_NAME}: ${APP_NAME_HI}`;\n 6 | \n 7 | export const APP_TAGLINE_EN =\n 8 |   \"The government checks your papers after you apply. KaagazCheck checks them before you apply, and tells you exactly what to fix.\";\n 9 | export const APP_TAGLINE_HI =\n10 |   \"सरकार आपके कागज़ आवेदन के बाद जाँचती है। कागज़ चेक उन्हें आवेदन से पहले जाँचता है और बताता है कि क्या ठीक करना है।\";","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\src\\core\\appInfo.test.ts","result":" 1 | import { describe, expect, it } from \"vitest\";\n 2 | import fc from \"fast-check\";\n 3 | import { z } from \"zod\";\n 4 | import {\n 5 |   APP_NAME,\n 6 |   APP_NAME_HI,\n 7 |   APP_TAGLINE_EN,\n 8 |   APP_TAGLINE_HI,\n 9 |   APP_TITLE,\n10 | } from \"./appInfo\";\n11 | \n12 | describe(\"appInfo (smoke)\", () => {\n13 |   it(\"has the exact bilingual title, with intact Devanagari\", () => {\n14 |     expect(APP_TITLE).toBe(\"KaagazCheck: कागज़ चेक\");\n15 |     expect(APP_NAME).toBe(\"KaagazCheck\");\n16 |     // \"कागज़\" with nukta: क ा ग ज ़\n17 |     expect(Array.from(APP_NAME_HI.normalize(\"NFD\")).slice(0, 5)).toEqual([\n18 |       \"\\u0915\",\n19 |       \"\\u093E\",\n20 |       \"\\u0917\",\n21 |       \"\\u091C\",\n22 |       \"\\u093C\",\n23 |     ]);\n24 |   });\n25 | \n26 |   it(\"taglines are non-empty and the Hindi one is in Devanagari\", () => {\n27 |     const schema = z.string().min(10);\n28 |     expect(schema.safeParse(APP_TAGLINE_EN).success).toBe(true);\n29 |     expect(schema.safeParse(APP_TAGLINE_HI).success).toBe(true);\n30 |     expect(/[\\u0900-\\u097F]/.test(APP_TAGLINE_HI)).toBe(true);\n31 |   });\n32 | \n33 |   it(\"test tooling works (fast-check property)\", () => {\n34 |     fc.assert(\n35 |       fc.property(fc.string(), (s) => `${s}${APP_TITLE}`.endsWith(APP_TITLE)),\n36 |     );\n37 |   });\n38 | });","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\src\\app\\layout.tsx","result":" 1 | import type { Metadata } from \"next\";\n 2 | import { Geist, Geist_Mono } from \"next/font/google\";\n 3 | import { APP_TAGLINE_EN, APP_TITLE } from \"@/core/appInfo\";\n 4 | import \"./globals.css\";\n 5 | \n 6 | const geistSans = Geist({\n 7 |   variable: \"--font-geist-sans\",\n 8 |   subsets: [\"latin\"],\n 9 | });\n10 | \n11 | const geistMono = Geist_Mono({\n12 |   variable: \"--font-geist-mono\",\n13 |   subsets: [\"latin\"],\n14 | });\n15 | \n16 | export const metadata: Metadata = {\n17 |   title: APP_TITLE,\n18 |   description: APP_TAGLINE_EN,\n19 | };\n20 | \n21 | export default function RootLayout({\n22 |   children,\n23 | }: Readonly<{ children: React.ReactNode }>) {\n24 |   return (\n25 |     <html\n26 |       lang=\"hi\"\n27 |       className={`${geistSans.variable} ${geistMono.variable} h-full antialiased`}\n28 |     >\n29 |       <body className=\"min-h-full flex flex-col\">{children}</body>\n30 |     </html>\n31 |   );\n32 | }","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\src\\app\\page.tsx","result":" 1 | import { APP_NAME, APP_NAME_HI, APP_TAGLINE_EN, APP_TAGLINE_HI } from \"@/core/appInfo\";\n 2 | \n 3 | export default function Home() {\n 4 |   return (\n 5 |     <main className=\"mx-auto flex w-full max-w-2xl flex-1 flex-col justify-center gap-6 px-6 py-16\">\n 6 |       <h1 className=\"text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight\">\n 7 |         {APP_NAME}: <span lang=\"hi\">{APP_NAME_HI}</span>\n 8 |       </h1>\n 9 |       <p lang=\"hi\" className=\"text-xl leading-8\">\n10 |         {APP_TAGLINE_HI}\n11 |       </p>\n12 |       <p lang=\"en\" className=\"text-lg leading-7 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400\">\n13 |         {APP_TAGLINE_EN}\n14 |       </p>\n15 |       <p className=\"text-sm text-zinc-500\">\n16 |         PM-KISAN · Orunodoi 3.0 (Assam) · Widow Pension (NSAP). Coming soon.\n17 |       </p>\n18 |     </main>\n19 |   );\n20 | }","success":true}],"durationMs":8}}
