{"ts":"2026-10-10T08:34:12.546Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"tool","toolName":"read_files","toolCallId":"toolu_01DAa1DCGEbPAeLMtEcmYKoZ","output":[{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\docs\\sample-notice-orunodoi-oct2026.md","result":" 1 | # Sample input for the Rule Maintenance Agent: a temporary payment change (demo)\n 2 | \n 3 | *Demo notice modelled on a reported October 2026 change (The Economic Times report of a one-time ₹1,500 Orunodoi payment for that month). Before quoting on slides, confirm against the official Government of Assam notification.*\n 4 | \n 5 | ---\n 6 | \n 7 | Orunodoi: For the month of October 2026, eligible beneficiaries will receive a one-time amount of Rs. 1,500 instead of the regular Rs. 1,250. From November 2026, the regular monthly amount of Rs. 1,250 continues.\n 8 | \n 9 | ---\n10 | \n11 | Expected agent behaviour: propose a new version of `orunodoi-3` with a time-bounded benefit override (effective 2026-10-01 to 2026-10-31, amount 1500), keep the recurring 1250, mark provenance as provisional until an official notice URL is added, write regression tests (October date → 1500, November date → 1250, eligibility checks unchanged), run all existing tests, and wait for human approval.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\techContext.md","result":" 1 | # Tech context\n 2 | \n 3 | ## Stack\n 4 | - One Next.js 16 app (App Router, `src/` dir, `@/*` → `./src/*`), React 19, TypeScript strict, Tailwind CSS v4 (via `@tailwindcss/turbopack` loader in `next.config.ts`).\n 5 | - Validation: zod 4.\n 6 | - Tests: Vitest 5 (Node environment, `src/**/*.test.ts`) + fast-check 4.\n 7 | - Lint: ESLint 9 flat config (`eslint-config-next`); `next lint` no longer exists in Next 16.\n 8 | - Database (T3): built-in `node:sqlite` (WAL); fall back to `better-sqlite3` only if needed. `node:sqlite` loads on this machine.\n 9 | - AI: Cline API (OpenAI-compatible), base URL `https://api.cline.bot/api/v1`, all calls via `src/server/ai.ts`.\n10 | - In-product agent (T3): `@cline/sdk` `Agent`, `providerId: \"openai-compatible\"`, tools via `createTool` with zod schemas.\n11 | \n12 | ## Environment\n13 | - Windows, PowerShell 5.1; the path contains a space (`C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build`). Use npm scripts and cross-platform Node code.\n14 | - Node v24.21.0, npm 11.19.0, git 2.55.0.\n15 | - Secrets only in `.env.local` (git-ignored): `CLINE_API_KEY`, `CLINE_MODEL` (e.g. `anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5`, never a `:batch` model). The template is `.env.example`.\n16 | - Write files containing Hindi with the editor tool (UTF-8), not PowerShell redirection.\n17 | \n18 | ## npm scripts\n19 | | Script | Command |\n20 | |---|---|\n21 | | `dev` | `next dev` |\n22 | | `build` | `next build` |\n23 | | `start` | `next start` |\n24 | | `lint` | `eslint .` |\n25 | | `typecheck` | `tsc --noEmit` |\n26 | | `test` | `vitest run` |\n27 | | `test:watch` | `vitest` |\n28 | \n29 | ## Gotchas found in T0\n30 | - Vitest 5 needs `@types/node` ≥ 22 (peer dep), so `@types/node` is `^22`.\n31 | - The Vitest config is `vitest.config.mts` (ESM); a `.ts` config triggers a Vite \"configLoader native\" warning because `package.json` has no `\"type\": \"module\"`.\n32 | - The global `LayoutProps<\"/\">` type only exists after `next build`/`next dev` generate `.next/types`, so `layout.tsx` uses an explicit `Readonly<{ children: React.ReactNode }>` to keep `npm run typecheck` working on a clean checkout.\n33 | - Vite writes warnings to stderr, which PowerShell reports as `NativeCommandError`. Check the real exit code (e.g. run via `cmd /c ... & echo %ERRORLEVEL%`).\n34 | - `npm install` is slow here (about 5 minutes for a fresh install); long commands can exceed the tool timeout, so run them in the background with logs.\n35 | \n36 | ## Scaffold notes\n37 | Generated with `create-next-app@16.4.0` in a temp folder and copied in (it refuses non-empty folders). Defaults kept: `cacheComponents: true`, `partialPrefetching: true`. `AGENTS.md` is written by Next (`next dev` re-adds it), so it is committed.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\vitest.config.mts","result":" 1 | import { fileURLToPath } from \"node:url\";\n 2 | import { defineConfig } from \"vitest/config\";\n 3 | \n 4 | export default defineConfig({\n 5 |   resolve: {\n 6 |     alias: {\n 7 |       \"@\": fileURLToPath(new URL(\"./src\", import.meta.url)),\n 8 |     },\n 9 |   },\n10 |   test: {\n11 |     environment: \"node\",\n12 |     include: [\"src/**/*.test.ts\"],\n13 |   },\n14 | });","success":true}],"durationMs":23}}
