{"ts":"2026-10-10T08:57:10.165Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"reasoning","reasoning":"I'm checking that wordScore stays symmetric across cases: different-length greedy pairing, equal-length jaroWinkler and sorted comparisons, and initialsOnly all preserve symmetry regardless of argument order.\n\nTesting specific name pairs through the algorithm — \"Ramesh\" vs \"Suresh\" computes a Jaro score around 0.778, below the 0.85 threshold, correctly flagging a mismatch. Similarly tracing through \"Sunita Devi\"/\"SUNITA DEBI\" and \"RAMESHKUMAR\"/\"Ramesh Kumar\" to confirm canonical joining and matching logic behaves as expected.\n\nI'm also checking reordering and initials cases (\"R K Sharma\" vs \"Ramesh Kumar Sharma\", \"SHARMA RAMESH KUMAR\") to make sure initials_only and possible_match detection work, then starting to trace Devanagari transliteration rules for \"रमेश कुमार शर्मा\" to confirm consonant-vowel combinations map correctly to Roman letters.\n\nContinuing the transliteration checks for Assamese and Bengali scripts (\"ৰমেশ\", \"সুনীতা দেবী\", \"শ্ৰীমতী\"), verifying they produce the correct canonical Roman forms, then confirming the nameMatch function correctly classifies \"सुनीता देवी\" vs \"Sunita Devi\" as a possible match through canonicalization.\n\nI'm also checking the invariant that normalizeName produces consistent tokenization so a name always matches itself, handling edge cases like filtered empty tokens, uppercase conversions of special characters like ß, and honorific stripping in examples like \"MR. R.K. Sharma\" and \"Late Shri Ram-Prasad\".\n\nScore symmetry holds for both equal and unequal-length word matching via the greedy approach, and identical names must always score exactly 1 within the [0,1] range. I'm confirming the evaluate test ensures only exact matches produce an \"ok\" result while possible matches never do, then continuing to append the remaining nameMatch logic.\n\n"}}
{"ts":"2026-10-10T08:57:10.170Z","type":"hook_event","hookEventName":"tool_call","agentId":"agent_51a9851e-3b11-4c38-b2a2-fdb716052990","taskId":"conv_1791620239910_z2g8z69","parentAgentId":null}
{"ts":"2026-10-10T08:57:10.171Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_start","contentType":"tool","toolName":"editor","toolCallId":"toolu_013ZSErkAbgbDNiCBRuu56xv","input":{"path":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\src\\core\\nameMatch.ts","insert_line":90,"new_text":"\nconst round3 = (x: number) => Math.round(x * 1000) / 1000;\nconst mean = (xs: number[]) => xs.reduce((s, x) => s + x, 0) / xs.length;\n\n/** Word-level similarity shown to the user for transparency (never a decision by itself). */\nfunction wordScore(a: string[], b: string[]): number {\n  if (a.length === b.length) {\n    const inOrder = mean(a.map((t, i) => jaroWinkler(t, b[i])));\n    const sa = [...a].sort();\n    const sb = [...b].sort();\n    const sorted = mean(sa.map((t, i) => jaroWinkler(t, sb[i])));\n    return Math.max(inOrder, sorted);\n  }\n  // Different word counts: greedy best pairing of the shorter list, divided by the longer length.\n  const [short, long] = a.length < b.length ? [a, b] : [b, a];\n  const used = new Array<boolean>(long.length).fill(false);\n  let total = 0;\n  for (const t of short) {\n    let best = -1;\n    let bestScore = 0;\n    long.forEach((u, i) => {\n      const s = jaroWinkler(t, u);\n      if (!used[i] && s > bestScore) {\n        best = i;\n        bestScore = s;\n      }\n    });\n    if (best >= 0) {\n      used[best] = true;\n      total += bestScore;\n    }\n  }\n  return total / long.length;\n}\n\nconst isInitialOf = (x: string, y: string) => x.length === 1 && y.length > 1 && y.startsWith(x);\n\n/** Same word count; at least one word is an initial of the other's word; the rest agree. */\nfunction initialsOnly(a: string[], b: string[]): boolean {\n  if (a.length !== b.length) return false;\n  let initials = 0;\n  for (let i = 0; i < a.length; i++) {\n    if (isInitialOf(a[i], b[i]) || isInitialOf(b[i], a[i])) initials++;\n    else if (a[i] !== b[i] && jaroWinkler(a[i], b[i]) < POSSIBLE_MATCH_THRESHOLD) return false;\n  }\n  return initials > 0;\n}\n\n/**\n * Compares two names.\n * - same: identical after formatting normalisation (case, punctuation, spaces, joined words, leading honorifics)\n * - possible_match: differs only by abbreviations/variants, transliteration, word order,\n *   or every word pair has Jaro-Winkler ≥ 0.85\n * - initials_only: some words are only initials of the other name's words\n * - mismatch: anything else (including a missing or extra word, or an empty name)\n */\nexport function nameMatch(a: string, b: string): NameMatchResult {\n  const ta = tokenize(a);\n  const tb = tokenize(b);\n  if (ta.length === 0 || tb.length === 0) return { level: \"mismatch\", score: 0 };\n\n  const rawA = ta.map((t) => t.raw).join(\"\");\n  const rawB = tb.map((t) => t.raw).join(\"\");\n  if (rawA === rawB) return { level: \"same\", score: 1 };\n\n  const ca = ta.map((t) => canonical(t.latin));\n  const cb = tb.map((t) => canonical(t.latin));\n  // Never report 1 for something that is not `same`.\n  const score = Math.min(0.999, round3(wordScore(ca, cb)));\n\n  if (ca.join(\"\") === cb.join(\"\")) return { level: \"possible_match\", score };\n  if (ca.length === cb.length && [...ca].sort().join(\" \") === [...cb].sort().join(\" \")) {\n    return { level: \"possible_match\", score };\n  }\n  if (initialsOnly(ca, cb)) return { level: \"initials_only\", score };\n  if (ca.length === cb.length && ca.every((t, i) => jaroWinkler(t, cb[i]) >= POSSIBLE_MATCH_THRESHOLD)) {\n    return { level: \"possible_match\", score };\n  }\n  return { level: \"mismatch\", score };\n}\n\nconst LEVEL_RANK: Record<NameMatchResult[\"level\"], number> = {\n  same: 3,\n  possible_match: 2,\n  initials_only: 1,\n  mismatch: 0,\n};\n\n/** The best match of `name` against several candidates (e.g. land-record co-owners). */\nexport function bestNameMatch(name: string, candidates: readonly string[]): NameMatchResult {\n  let best: NameMatchResult = { level: \"mismatch\", score: 0 };\n  for (const c of candidates) {\n    const m = nameMatch(name, c);\n    if (LEVEL_RANK[m.level] > LEVEL_RANK[best.level] || (m.level === best.level && m.score > best.score)) best = m;\n  }\n  return best;\n}\n"}}}
