{"ts":"2026-10-10T09:06:21.875Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"reasoning","reasoning":"All tests passed, so now I'm moving on to designing evaluate.ts and samples.ts, planning out date validation, a helper to find the first document of a given type, a low-confidence threshold of 0.8 for flagging verification needs, and checks for mandatory document presence.\n\nFor name checks, I'm comparing each document's name field against the scheme's reference document — if the target document isn't present it's not_applicable since the missing-doc check already handles that case, and if a present document is missing its name field entirely, it should trigger needs_verification since we can't confirm the match.\n\nMatch levels map onto outcomes: same → ok; possible_match or initials_only → needs_verification; mismatch → action_required, unless there's an answered family-owner question, in which case it drops to needs_verification. I'm also treating any low-confidence read as needs_verification regardless of match level, since the user should confirm a name we might have misread.\n\nFor field-level checks, absent documents are not_applicable, missing or low-confidence values trigger needs_verification with a \"couldn't read\" message, and I'm normalizing values by stripping spaces/hyphens and uppercasing before comparing.\n\nFor age eligibility: missing or invalid dob triggers needs_verification, dob after the as-of date is needs_verification, in-range is ok, and out-of-range depends on provenance — verified becomes action_required (not_eligible) while provisional stays needs_verification, with a note appended when above the max. Requirements follow similar logic (true→ok, false+verified→action_required, false+provisional→needs_verification, unanswered→needs_verification), and the anyOf check aggregates across its questions using the shared provenance to decide ok/action_required/needs_verification.\n\nFor exclusions and external checks, I'm applying the same verified/provisional/unanswered pattern, with external checks always resolving to needs_verification. Overall eligibility rolls up from eligibility-kind checks (action_required→not_eligible, needs_verification→needs_verification, else likely_eligible), reported separately from readiness, which escalates to action_required if any non-external check requires action, otherwise to needs_verification if any remain unresolved.\n\nI'm now tracing through the Orunodoi test case, confirming document and name matches (ration card, Aadhaar, bank name all consistent for Anjali Bora) to verify the readiness status lands on ready_for_review as expected.\n\nFor the widow test, I check all four documents (Aadhaar, bank, BPL proof, death certificate), confirming name consistency and age/widow/BPL requirements pass, resulting in a ready status.\n\nThen I move to the PM-KISAN clean case, noting that the family-owner land question goes unanswered since it isn't present in that applicant's data, which only matters when there's a mismatch to resolve.\n\nI'm also confirming that the \"ready iff no blocking non-external checks\" property holds by construction, and working through the edge case where a name like \"Smt.\" alone normalizes to an empty token set — this should trigger either a mismatch or a \"couldn't read name\" verification state, either of which satisfies the property that a possible match is never marked fully okay.\n\nFor the report itself, I'm structuring it with a disclaimer, benefit eligibility from benefitOn, and supporting document statuses using the DOC_LABELS for display. I'm drafting bilingual messages for each outcome type, making sure the possible-match message includes a note that officials may still reject it, and the provisional exclusion message references the correct confirmation location via FIX_WHERE_LABELS tied to the scheme's confirmAt field.\n\nI'm checking the age-80 message includes \"Old Age Pension\" and that similarity scores like \"0.93\" are shown for transparency, while making sure no Aadhaar numbers, 12-digit account numbers, or other sensitive identifiers leak into the report or messages. I'm also verifying the report conforms to the schema with proper rule provenance, and confirming every check includes a fixWhere value.\n\nFor passing checks I'll set fixWhere to \"none\" since it still needs to be truthy, while failing checks like missing land records get a real fixWhere such as circle_office. I'm making sure every messageAs field contains actual Assamese script characters to satisfy the test requirement. For the sample cases, I'm drafting Sample A as a clean PM-KISAN case, Sample B with KYC issues on bank and land records for a fictional person, and Sample C as a widow missing a death certificate, using fake names throughout.\n\nI'm giving Sample C a realistic DOB around 1968 and standard documents like aadhaar, bank, and BPL proof, while adding confidence scores to each sample so Sample A clears the 0.8 threshold and shows ready_for_review status. I'm also exporting a LOW_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD constant set to 0.8, then planning to write evaluate.ts across two chunks to stay under the character limit.\n\n"}}
{"ts":"2026-10-10T09:06:21.879Z","type":"hook_event","hookEventName":"tool_call","agentId":"agent_51a9851e-3b11-4c38-b2a2-fdb716052990","taskId":"conv_1791620239910_z2g8z69","parentAgentId":null}
{"ts":"2026-10-10T09:06:21.880Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_start","contentType":"tool","toolName":"editor","toolCallId":"toolu_01HUehATfGaFB6wv577k9KPA","input":{"path":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\src\\core\\evaluate.ts","new_text":"// The deterministic rule engine: evaluate(scheme, docs, answers, asOfDate) → Report. Pure.\n// Two verdicts (eligibility, readiness). Provisional rules and external facts never decide; they\n// return needs_verification. A fuzzy name score never becomes `ok`; only `same` does.\nimport { ageOn } from \"./age\";\nimport { benefitOn } from \"./benefit\";\nimport { assertIsoDate, isIsoDate } from \"./dates\";\nimport { DISCLAIMER, DOC_LABELS, FIX_WHERE_LABELS } from \"./labels\";\nimport { bestNameMatch, normalizeName } from \"./nameMatch\";\nimport type {\n  Answers,\n  Check,\n  DocType,\n  Eligibility,\n  ExtractedDoc,\n  FieldName,\n  NameCheckRule,\n  Question,\n  Readiness,\n  Report,\n  RuleProvenance,\n  SchemeRule,\n} from \"./types\";\n\n/** A field read with confidence below this must be confirmed by the user. */\nexport const LOW_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD = 0.8;\n\ntype Draft = Omit<Check, \"provenance\"> & { provenance: RuleProvenance };\n\nconst docLabel = (d: DocType) => DOC_LABELS[d];\nconst where = (w: Check[\"fixWhere\"]) => FIX_WHERE_LABELS[w];\n\nfunction findDoc(docs: readonly ExtractedDoc[], docType: DocType): ExtractedDoc | undefined {\n  return docs.find((d) => d.docType === docType);\n}\n\nfunction isLowConfidence(doc: ExtractedDoc, field: FieldName): boolean {\n  const c = doc.confidence[field];\n  return c !== undefined && c < LOW_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD;\n}\n\n// ---------- documents ----------\nfunction mandatoryDocChecks(scheme: SchemeRule, docs: readonly ExtractedDoc[]): Draft[] {\n  return scheme.mandatoryDocs.map((req) => {\n    const label = docLabel(req.docType);\n    const present = findDoc(docs, req.docType) !== undefined;\n    const commonly = req.provenance.status === \"provisional\";\n    return present\n      ? {\n          id: `doc_${req.docType}`,\n          kind: \"document\",\n          docType: req.docType,\n          result: \"ok\",\n          messageEn: `${cap(label.en)} added.`,\n          messageAs: `${label.as} যোগ কৰা হৈছে।`,\n          fixWhere: \"none\",\n          provenance: req.provenance,\n        }\n      : {\n          id: `doc_${req.docType}`,\n          kind: \"document\",\n          docType: req.docType,\n          result: \"action_required\",\n          messageEn:\n            `Missing: ${label.en}. Get it from ${where(req.fixWhere).en} and add it before you apply.` +\n            (commonly ? \" (Commonly required; confirm locally.)\" : \"\"),\n          messageAs:\n            `নাই: ${label.as}। আবেদন কৰাৰ আগতে ${where(req.fixWhere).as}ৰ পৰা লৈ যোগ কৰক।` +\n            (commonly ? \" (সাধাৰণতে লাগে; স্থানীয়ভাৱে নিশ্চিত কৰক।)\" : \"\"),\n          fixWhere: req.fixWhere,\n          provenance: req.provenance,\n        };\n  });\n}\n\n// ---------- names ----------\nfunction nameCheck(scheme: SchemeRule, rule: NameCheckRule, docs: readonly ExtractedDoc[], answers: Answers): Draft {\n  const id = `name_${rule.docType}`;\n  const target = findDoc(docs, rule.docType);\n  const reference = findDoc(docs, scheme.nameReference);\n  const tLabel = docLabel(rule.docType);\n  const rLabel = docLabel(scheme.nameReference);\n  const base = { id, kind: \"name\" as const, docType: rule.docType, provenance: rule.provenance };\n\n  if (!target || !reference) {\n    return {\n      ...base,\n      result: \"not_applicable\",\n      messageEn: `Name on the ${tLabel.en} not compared: the ${(target ? rLabel : tLabel).en} is not added.`,\n      messageAs: `${tLabel.as}ৰ নাম মিলোৱা হোৱা নাই: ${(target ? rLabel : tLabel).as} যোগ কৰা হোৱা নাই।`,\n      fixWhere: \"none\",\n    };\n  }\n\n  const refName = reference.fields.name ?? \"\";\n  const names = rule.field === \"ownerNames\" ? (target.fields.ownerNames ?? []) : [target.fields.name ?? \"\"];\n  const readable = names.filter((n) => normalizeName(n) !== \"\");\n  if (normalizeName(refName) === \"\" || readable.length === 0) {\n    const which = normalizeName(refName) === \"\" ? rLabel : tLabel;\n    return {\n      ...base,\n      result: \"needs_verification\",\n      messageEn: `We could not read the name on the ${which.en}. Please type it exactly as printed.`,\n      messageAs: `${which.as}ত থকা নামটো আমি পঢ়িব নোৱাৰিলোঁ। ছপা হোৱাৰ দৰে হুবহু লিখক।`,\n      fixWhere: \"applicant\",\n    };\n  }\n\n  const match = bestNameMatch(refName, readable);\n  const scoreTxt = match.score.toFixed(2);\n  const lowConf = isLowConfidence(reference, \"name\") || isLowConfidence(target, rule.field);\n  if (lowConf) {\n    return {\n      ...base,\n      match,\n      result: \"needs_verification\",\n      messageEn: `We are not sure we read the name on the ${tLabel.en} or ${rLabel.en} correctly. Please check it and correct it if needed.`,\n      messageAs: `${tLabel.as} বা ${rLabel.as}ত থকা নামটো আমি শুদ্ধকৈ পঢ়িছোঁ নে নাই নিশ্চিত নহয়। পৰীক্ষা কৰি প্ৰয়োজন হ'লে শুধৰাওক।`,\n      fixWhere: \"applicant\",\n    };\n  }\n\n  switch (match.level) {\n    case \"same\":\n      return {\n        ...base,\n        match,\n        result: \"ok\",\n        messageEn: `Name on the ${tLabel.en} matches the ${rLabel.en}.`,\n        messageAs: `${tLabel.as}ৰ নাম ${rLabel.as}ৰ সৈতে মিলে।`,\n        fixWhere: \"none\",\n      };\n    case \"possible_match\":\n    case \"initials_only\": {\n      const initials = match.level === \"initials_only\";\n      return {\n        ...base,\n        match,\n        result: \"needs_verification\",\n        messageEn:\n          (initials\n            ? `The name on the ${tLabel.en} uses initials instead of the full name on the ${rLabel.en} (similarity ${scoreTxt}). `\n            : `The names on the ${tLabel.en} and ${rLabel.en} look like the same person written differently (similarity ${scoreTxt}). `) +\n          `Officials may still reject this. Ask ${where(rule.fixWhere).en} to make them identical.`,\n        messageAs:\n          (initials\n            ? `${tLabel.as}ত ${rLabel.as}ৰ সম্পূৰ্ণ নামৰ সলনি আদ্যাক্ষৰ ব্যৱহাৰ কৰা হৈছে (মিল ${scoreTxt})। `\n            : `${tLabel.as} আৰু ${rLabel.as}ৰ নাম একেজন ব্যক্তিৰ বেলেগকৈ লিখা যেন লাগে (মিল ${scoreTxt})। `) +\n          `বিষয়াই তথাপিও নাকচ কৰিব পাৰে। দুয়োটা হুবহু একে কৰিবলৈ ${where(rule.fixWhere).as}ত কওক।`,\n        fixWhere: rule.fixWhere,\n      };\n    }\n    case \"mismatch\":\n      return familyOwnedOrMismatch(base, rule, answers, match, tLabel, rLabel, scoreTxt);\n  }\n}\n"}}}
