{"ts":"2026-10-10T09:08:37.943Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"reasoning","reasoning":"Now I'm working out the eligibility determination logic: if any verified eligibility check (age, requirements, anyOf, exclusions) comes back action_required, the result is not_eligible; otherwise if any check needs verification, it's needs_verification; otherwise likely_eligible—documents don't factor into eligibility itself. I'm also starting to define readiness separately, based on whether any check of any kind requires action.\n\nChecking test cases against this logic: income tax payer triggering action_required readiness works, and PM-KISAN unanswered exclusions producing needs_verification for both eligibility and readiness also holds up fine. I'm confirming the property that ready_for_review happens exactly when no non-external check is action_required or needs_verification, and verifying Orunodoi never resolves to not_eligible—provisional or unanswered questions there only ever produce needs_verification, same with NFSA requirements answered \"no\".\n\nFor the widow pension case, I'm checking several scenarios: verified age failure should yield action_required and not_eligible, while low-confidence DOB, missing aadhaar, invalid DOB strings, and DOB falling after the asOfDate should all safely resolve to needs_verification rather than throwing errors. I'm also checking that the age-80 not_eligible case correctly references the Old Age Pension scheme in its message.\n\nNow I'm working through requirement question logic: answered-false-plus-verified gives action_required/not_eligible, answered-false-plus-provisional and unanswered both give needs_verification, and answered-true passes as ok. For anyOf checks, an empty list skips, any true answer passes using that question's provenance, all-false-verified gives action_required, all-false-provisional gives needs_verification, and unanswered-with-no-true gives needs_verification using the first question's provenance.\n\nFor exclusion checks, I'm mapping out the branches: yes+verified gives action_required with a not-eligible message citing the label, yes+provisional gives needs_verification with a confirmation prompt, unanswered gives needs_verification, and no passes as ok. External checks always resolve to needs_verification with kind \"external.\" I'm also defining the exact message text for verified exclusions, along with fixWhere logic that falls back to the scheme's confirmAt, or \"none\" for ok checks.\n\nI'm verifying test constraints: fixWhere \"none\" counts as truthy, all messages must contain Assamese script (confirming sample ok-check and field messages do), no message leaks a full Aadhaar number, and the sample 11-digit account number is safe. I'm also checking ID conventions for each check type (excl_, req_, age, anyof, ext_), confirming supporting docs map correctly to presence status, and verifying the PM-KISAN pack's JSON doesn't accidentally match forbidden land-related regex patterns, plus confirming the regression test comparing two reports holds since land area isn't included. Now I'm ready to write the third chunk.\n\n"}}
