{"ts":"2026-10-10T09:10:57.284Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"reasoning","reasoning":"That race condition with the build running alongside my temp file operations explains the inconsistency — I should rerun the build in isolation. Looking at the spot results, the scores seem reasonable: the near-1.0 match for \"Smt. Sunita Devi\" vs \"SUNITA DEBI\" reflects canonicalization working as intended, even if it's slightly misleading on its face. I'll accept these results.\n\nI also realize my EXIT code capture is broken — %ERRORLEVEL% expands at parse time inside `cmd /c`, so it always prints EXIT=0 regardless of actual failure. That means the typecheck/lint EXIT=0 readings could be unreliable too, though since their outputs showed no errors, they're probably fine. I should switch to using `&& echo OK || echo FAIL` for accurate success/failure detection going forward.\n\nThe earlier failure was just a timing conflict with my temporary spot-check script that got deleted mid-typecheck, and the `EXIT=0` report was misleading since `%ERRORLEVEL%` expands before the command runs. I'll rerun build, typecheck, and lint sequentially with accurate pass/fail reporting.\n\n"}}
